{"name":"Festive Bordeaux","hex":"#6e0f12","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"festive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the atmosphere, decoration, or attitude of a festival, holiday, or celebration.","In the mood to celebrate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/festive"},{"term":"bordeaux","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Bordeaux (“fungicide; wine”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bordeaux"}],"entries":[{"title":"Festival","blocks":[{"text":"A festival is an event celebrated by a community and centred on one or more characteristic aspects of its religion, traditions or cultures. It is often observed as an indigenous or national holiday, a religious celebration, or a cultural fair (mela). A festival is a typical case of glocalization, and also reflects the high culture-low culture interrelationship. In addition to religion and folklore, a significant source for festivals has been agriculture. Since, food is such an essential resource, many festivals are associated with harvest time. Religious observances and thanksgiving for good harvests are integrated into celebrations that take place in autumn, such as Halloween in the northern hemisphere and Easter in the southern hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Holi_Festival_of_Colors_Utah%2C_United_States_2013.jpg/330px-Holi_Festival_of_Colors_Utah%2C_United_States_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Festival"},{"title":"Bordeaux","blocks":[{"text":"Bordeaux is a city on the river Garonne in the Gironde department, southwestern France. A port city, it is the capital of the Nouvelle-Aquitaine region, as well as the prefecture of the Gironde department. Its inhabitants are called \"Bordelais\" (masculine) or \"Bordelaises\" (feminine). The term \"Bordelais\" may also refer to the city and its surrounding region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bordeaux_Place_de_la_Bourse_de_nuit.jpg/330px-Bordeaux_Place_de_la_Bourse_de_nuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bordeaux"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg/500px-Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg/1280px-Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg/500px-Weezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Musikfest, an eleven-day outdoor music festival held annually each August in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, is the largest free music festival in the United States, drawing over 1.3 million attendees.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWeezer_Bethlehem_2019_5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Red_and_Gold_for_Ni%C3%B1o.jpg/500px-Red_and_Gold_for_Ni%C3%B1o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Red_and_Gold_for_Ni%C3%B1o.jpg/1280px-Red_and_Gold_for_Ni%C3%B1o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign